      safety="Feet are walls and walls do not move: the planted-feet law is the safety system as well as the game, because a child stepping into the road meets a rolling ball at ankle height and another wall-keeper's legs at the same moment — so the ball is rolled only from a kneel, two hands, at true rolling pace, and any ball that starts travelling fast ends the journey: it is caught by the adult and the roll restarts from the gate, kindly, without a lecture. The road is walked and cleared by the adult before every session, wall-keepers stand a full arm from the rows opposite them, and nobody lies, sits, or crawls in the road at any time, for any reason — the tunnel is walked around, always, by everyone, the roller included.",
